FADE IN:

EXT. ANTARCTICA - SUNSET

SUPER: "BYRD, 1934: ANTARCTICA"

BYRD, alone in the vast, isolated Antarctic winter. Not a soul in sight.

Sunset incoming.

Byrd, ill, violently COUGHING his guts out.

He cooks a large piece of meat on the fire.

He takes the meat off and begins to eat it, facing the desolate area of nothingness.

Pause.

Byrd, just eating the meat.

Just as he is about to go to his tent, five meters away, he sees a FLICKER on the horizon.

Byrd looks startled. A tad uncertain.

In his eyes, you see his motivation to conquer the unknown in the distance.

The camera turns off Byrd, panning 90 degrees from side-on, to just the endless ice desert.

The remoteness sinks in.

CUT TO:

> **ADMIRAL BYRD: BEYOND THE ICE** <
